<title>MALAYSIA: RESEARCH ALERT-Morgan Stanley downgrades Malaysia.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Morgan Stanley downgrades Malaysia.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. investment bank Morgan Stanley Dean Witter said it is lowering its weighting on Malaysia by one percentage point to seven percent.</p>
<p>&quot;We are already underweight Malaysia and are now reducing the weighting further to seven percent,&quot; said Morgan Stanley.</p>
<p>The main reasons for the company's decision included the recent devaluation in the Thai baht.</p>
<p>&quot;The two countries most likely to be affected are the Philippines and Malaysia,&quot; said Morgan Stanley.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-206 2323)</p>
</text>
